0001 | === {{Lemma|Image of Frame under Frame Homomorphism is Frame|1|Lemma 1}} ===
0002 | Let $T \subseteq S_3$.
0003 | 
0004 | Let $\bigvee T$ denote the [[Definition:Supremum of Set|supremum]] of $T$ in $L_2$.
0005 | 
0006 | Then:
0007 | :$\bigvee T \in S_3$.{{qed|lemma}}
0008 | 
0009 | === {{Lemma|Image of Frame under Frame Homomorphism is Frame|2|Lemma 2}} ===
0010 | Let $F \subseteq S_3$ be a [[Definition:Finite Subset|finite subset]].
0011 | 
0012 | Let $\bigwedge F$ denote the [[Definition:Infimum of Set|infimum]] of $F$ in $L_2$.
0013 | 
0014 | Then:
0015 | :$\bigwedge F \in S_3$.{{qed|lemma}}
0016 | 
0017 | {{recall|Frame Homomorphism}}
0018 | Let $L_1 = \struct {S_1, \preceq_1}$ and $L_2 = \struct {S_2, \preceq_2}$ be [[Definition:Frame (Lattice Theory)|frames]].
0019 | 
0020 | Let $\phi: S_1 \to S_2$ be a [[Definition:Mapping|mapping]] between the underlying [[Definition:Set|sets]] of $L_1$ and $L_2$.
0021 | 
0022 | Then:
0023 | :$\phi$ is a '''[[Definition:Frame Homomorphism|frame homomorphism]]''', denoted $\phi: L_1 \to L_2$
0024 | {{iff}}:
0025 | :$\phi$ is [[Definition:Finite Meet Preserving Mapping|finite meet preserving]] and [[Definition:Arbitrary Join Preserving Mapping|arbitrary join preserving]]
0026 | 
0027 | === $\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 }$ is Arbitrary Join Preserving ===
0028 | 
0029 | Let $A \subseteq S_3$.
0030 | 
0031 | We have:
0032 | {{begin-eqn}}
0033 | {{eqn | l = \map {\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 } } { {\bigvee}_1 A}
0034 |       | r = \map \phi { {\bigvee}_1 A}
0035 |       | c = {{Defof|Restriction of Mapping}}
0036 | }}
0037 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_2 \phi \sqbrk A
0038 |       | c = {{Defof|Frame Homomorphism}}
0039 | }}
0040 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_3 \phi \sqbrk A
0041 |       | c = {{Lemma|Image of Frame under Frame Homomorphism is Frame|1|Lemma 1}}
0042 | }}
0043 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_3 \phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 } \sqbrk A
0044 |       | c = {{Defof|Restriction of Mapping}}
0045 | }}
0046 | {{end-eqn}}
0047 | 
0048 | where ${\bigvee}_1, {\bigvee}_2, {\bigvee}_3$ denotes the [[Definition:Supremum of Set|supremum]] in $L_1, L_2, L_3$ respectively.
0049 | 
0050 | It follows that $\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 }$ is [[Definition:Arbitrary Join Preserving Mapping|arbitrary join preserving]] by definition.
0051 | {{qed|lemma}}
0052 | 
0053 | === $\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 }$ is Finite Meet Preserving ===
0054 | 
0055 | Let $F \subseteq S_3$ be a [[DefinitiOn:Finite Set|finite set]].
0056 | 
0057 | We have:
0058 | {{begin-eqn}}
0059 | {{eqn | l = \map {\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 } } { {\bigwedge}_1 F}
0060 |       | r = \map \phi { {\bigwedge}_1 F}
0061 |       | c = {{Defof|Restriction of Mapping}}
0062 | }}
0063 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_2 \phi \sqbrk F
0064 |       | c = {{Defof|Frame Homomorphism}}
0065 | }}
0066 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_3 \phi \sqbrk F
0067 |       | c = {{Lemma|Image of Frame under Frame Homomorphism is Frame|2|Lemma 2}}
0068 | }}
0069 | {{eqn | r = {\bigwedge}_3 \phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 } \sqbrk F
0070 |       | c = {{Defof|Restriction of Mapping}}
0071 | }}
0072 | {{end-eqn}}
0073 | 
0074 | where ${\bigwedge}_1, {\bigwedge}_2, {\bigwedge}_3$ denotes the [[Definition:Infimum of Set|infimum]] in $L_1, L_2, L_3$ respectively.
0075 | 
0076 | It follows that $\phi \restriction_{S_1 \times S_3 }$ is [[Definition:Finite Meet Preserving Mapping|finite meet preserving]] by definition.
0077 | {{qed|lemma}}
0078 | 
0079 | The result follows.
0080 | {{qed}}
